cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the paper below together with the prior work it
  credits (see the priority note at the top of the paper).
title: "A machine-checked spectral floor for Pauli contextuality"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Donahue
    given-names: "Alexander S."
    alias: 0thernes
    affiliation: "0thernes LLC"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/hoggar-bound-lab"
url: "https://0thernes.github.io/hoggar-bound-lab/"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization, for every number of qubits and arbitrary sets of Pauli observables,
  of the spectral lower bound on the contextuality degree (first posted by B. W. Jonah,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23538829), with formally verified numerical corollaries, an independent
  reproduction of the known values for two to five qubits, and a demonstration on the
  Tsotchke stack (Moonlab, quantum_geometric_tensor, quantum_rng, Eshkol).
keywords:
  - quantum contextuality
  - Pauli group
  - symplectic polar space
  - Kochen-Specker theorem
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
